--TEST--
`Core\Http\Client::patch` sends the verb its own name spells, and `::request` sends the `Core\Http\Method` it is handed — including the verbs no row is named after — `rule:http-server/no-spelling-for-an-unbounded-wait`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The claim is *agreement*: the verb on the wire is asked of both halves of the
// class — the row whose name is the verb, and the row that is handed one — and
// read back off the record rather than off the call, so a member sending the
// verb it was named after by accident still fails here. Nothing below is
// granted `net.connect` and no socket is opened
// (`rule:testing/an-outbound-call-is-answered-from-a-table`).
Core\Test::answerHttp("https://api.example.com/*", 200, {body: "ok"});

// The named row. `patch` is the sixth verb this class spells, and a `PATCH` is
// a `POST`'s neighbour under `rule:http-server/a-non-idempotent-retry-needs-an-idempotency-key`.
var $named = Core\Http\Client::patch("https://api.example.com/orders/7", {json: ["status" => "paid"]});

// The same request through the row that takes the verb as an argument: there is
// no request object, and the bag is the one every other row takes.
var $handed = Core\Http\Client::request(Core\Http\Method::Patch, "https://api.example.com/orders/7", {json: ["status" => "paid"]});

// And the verbs `Core\Http\Method` has that this class is not named after,
// which is the whole reason the row exists — the last one chosen at run time,
// so no call site here spells it.
var $options = Core\Http\Client::request(Core\Http\Method::Options, "https://api.example.com/orders/7");
var $trace = Core\Http\Client::request(Core\Http\Method::Trace, "https://api.example.com/orders/7");
Core\Http\Method $chosen = Core\Http\Method::Delete;
var $dynamic = Core\Http\Client::request($chosen, "https://api.example.com/orders/7");

// One line per record: the verb's ordinal, then what the call carried. The two
// `Patch` records agree on every one of them.
var $sent = Core\Test::sentHttp();
foreach ($sent as Core\Test\SentRequest $call) {
    echo ($call->method() as int), " ", $call->header("content-type") ?? "-", " ", Core\Bytes::length($call->body()), "\n";
}
--EXPECT--
6 application/json 17
6 application/json 17
2 - 0
3 - 0
7 - 0
